<body>
    <h1>AI-1036: Metasight, an Object Intelligence Platform</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>This epic outlines the architecture for the Metasight Object Int=
elligence Platform. The system's goal is to transform a raw video archive i=
nto a powerful, searchable knowledge base.</p>
<p>The core strategy is a hybrid AI approach, utilizing two distinct, state=
-of-the-art models to enrich video data. This provides both rich, human-rea=
dable metadata and best-in-class visual search capabilities. The architectu=
re is designed as a scalable, event-driven system of microservices.</p>
<p>Existing object detection systems often generate a high rate of false po=
sitives from dynamic environmental factors like swaying trees or changing s=
hadows. This leads to alert fatigue and reduces the reliability of automate=
d monitoring.</p>
<p></p>
<p>The foundational strategy is to implement a two-stage process to add a l=
ayer of "common sense" to detection:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Contextual Analysis:</strong> First, a Vision-Language Model (VL=
M) analyzes the scene to provide a high-level, semantic understanding (e.g.=
, <em>"This is a backyard with trees swaying in the wind"</em>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Informed Detection:</strong> This contextual understanding is th=
en used to dynamically tune the parameters of a primary object detector. Fo=
r example, if "swaying trees" are identified, the confidence threshold for =
detecting a "person" can be raised to prevent misclassification of moving b=
ranches.</p></li>
</ol>
<p></p>
<p>The platform's long-term vision evolves from a real-time alerting system=
 into a persistent, searchable intelligence archive. The goal is to empower=
 a user to instantly find any object or event across the entire video histo=
ry.</p>
<p>An analyst needs to query the system with complex, natural-language ques=
tions or visual examples to find specific moments, such as:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><em>"Show me all instances of a delivery truck in the driveway last week=
."</em></p></li>
<li>
<p><em>"Find every appearance of this specific person across all cameras."<=
/em></p></li>
</ul>
<p>To enable this, every detected object must be enriched with detailed met=
adata and indexed for fast, multi-modal search.</p>
<h1 id=3D"AI-1036:Metasight,anObjectIntelligencePlatform-Metasight"><strong=
>Metasight</strong></h1>
<p>Metasight converts sampled video frames into structured, search-ready re=
cords by orchestrating Florence-2 for descriptive, task-prompted analysis a=
nd DINOv3 for universal visual features, then packaging both into a single =
record for indexing in Milvus. This implements our two-stage strategy and s=
upports a searchable intelligence archive rather than a detector-only syste=
m.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>A frame arrives from the upstream sampler with metadata (video_id, times=
tamp, source_uri).</p></li>
<li>
<p>Metasight performs:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Step 1: Florence-2 task processing (dense region captioning, object dete=
ction, optional OCR/grounding).</p></li>
<li>
<p>Step 2: DINOv3 feature extraction for frame and optional ROI/bbox embedd=
ings.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Optional Step 3: context-aware validation to reduce false positives.</p>=
</li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Metasight assembles a canonical record and writes to Milvus collections.=
</p></li>
</ol>
<p></p>
<p>The Metasight service is the core of the intelligence platform, transfor=
ming raw video frames into structured, searchable records. <sup> </sup>It a=
ccomplishes this by orchestrating two specialized AI models: Florence-2 for=
 descriptive, task-prompted analysis, and DINOv3 for generating universal v=
isual features. Metasight then packages the outputs from both models into a=
 single, comprehensive record for indexing in a Milvus vector database. Thi=
s two-stage strategy supports the platform's evolution from a simple detect=
or into a searchable intelligence archive.</p>
<h2 id=3D"AI-1036:Metasight,anObjectIntelligencePlatform-SystemFlowandConte=
xt"><strong>System Flow and Context</strong></h2>
<p>The overall workflow begins when a video frame, along with its associate=
d metadata (such as <code>video_id</code> and <code>timestamp</code>), arri=
ves from the video processor. Metasight then executes a multi-step enrichme=
nt process. First, it performs task-based processing with Florence-2, runni=
ng prompts for dense region captioning, object detection, and optional task=
s like OCR or phrase grounding. Next, it uses DINOv3 for feature extraction=
, generating a powerful embedding for the entire frame and, if configured, =
for specific regions of interest or bounding boxes within it.</p>
<p>An optional third step involves context-aware validation, which applies =
spatial, temporal, and semantic checks to the detected objects to reduce fa=
lse positives. <sup> </sup>Finally, Metasight assembles all generated data =
into a canonical record and writes it to the appropriate Milvus collections=
. It's important to note that while Metasight is designed to integrate with=
 a broader event-driven architecture, concerns like real-time alerting and =
downstream API consumption are considered out of scope for this core compon=
ent.</p>
<h2 id=3D"AI-1036:Metasight,anObjectIntelligencePlatform-ComponentDesign"><=
strong>Component Design</strong></h2>
<p>Metasight is responsible for accepting video frames and their minimal me=
tadata, running the Florence-2 and DINOv3 models to produce their respectiv=
e outputs, and applying the optional validation pass. It then emits canonic=
al records formatted for efficient, batch-friendly insertion into Milvus. T=
he service communicates with other internal components via HTTP/JSON, with =
the potential for asynchronous input and output through a RabbitMQ topic in=
 the future.</p>
<p>Logically, Metasight is composed of several internal components. A Prepr=
ocessor converts incoming image data into batched tensors and performs on-G=
PU resizing and normalization. The Object Detection and Indexing Process in=
terface with the Triton server to manage the distinct contracts for Florenc=
e-2 and DINOv3. A Validator component encapsulates the logic for spatial, t=
emporal, and semantic consistency checks. Finally, an Assembler merges the =
outputs from all previous stages, assigns unique IDs, and prepares the data=
 for the Milvus collections.</p>
<p>The processing sequence begins by receiving a batch of frames, which are=
 then run through the DINOv3 model once to produce universal feature embedd=
ings. These features are then reused where supported for the various Floren=
ce-2 tasks, such as object detection and dense region captioning. A compreh=
ensive list of detections is built, which includes the class, confidence sc=
ore, bounding box, descriptive attributes, and the associated frame and bou=
nding box embeddings. If enabled, the validation logic is applied before th=
e final records are emitted for indexing.</p>
<h2 id=3D"AI-1036:Metasight,anObjectIntelligencePlatform-ObjectDetection">O=
bject Detection</h2>
<p>This service is the core of the system. It receives a batch of video fra=
mes and orchestrates a sequence of AI calls via the NVIDIA Triton server.</=
p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Input:</strong> A message containing a raw video frame (e.g., HW=
C, UINT8 NumPy array).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Step 1: Descriptive Analysis (Florence-2)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> The frame is sent to the Florence-2 model.</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p><strong>Task:</strong> The model is prompted with a task like <code>"&lt=
;DENSE_REGION_CAPTION&gt;"</code>.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Output:</strong> A structured JSON object containing a list of a=
ll detected objects, each with its bounding box, a simple label, and a deta=
iled, human-readable caption. This output provides the rich, descriptive me=
tadata.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Step 2: Feature Extraction (DINOv3)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> The same frame is sent to the DINOv3 model.</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Task:</strong> The model processes the image to extract its deep=
 visual features.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Output:</strong> A single, high-dimensional image embedding vect=
or. This vector is a mathematical signature of the frame's visual content, =
optimized for similarity search.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"AI-1036:Metasight,anObjectIntelligencePlatform-IndexingProcess"><=
strong>Indexing Process</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Input:</strong> The JSON metadata from Florence-2 and the image =
embedding vector from DINOv3.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> The service assembles these two pieces of data,=
 along with source information (video path, timestamp), into a single, comp=
rehensive record.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Output:</strong> This record is inserted into the Milvus databas=
e.</p></li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"9c=
9f544d-f6f4-41c0-9731-a9c088c5a8e1" class=3D"confluenceTable">
